## 10. Training, validation and leakage prevention

**Split (whole profiles, deterministic, saved in `artifacts/split_manifest.json`).**

{{table_splits}}

Profiles are sorted by peak winding temperature, cut into chunks of {{chunk}} and each chunk contributes one
validation and one test profile (seeded). Only whole profiles move between sets; peak temperature is used only
to place profiles, not samples. Test profiles: {{test_ids}}. Validation profiles: {{val_ids}}.

**Guards.** (1) `forbidden_features` in the config + `assert_no_forbidden` on every feature list;
(2) the split manifest asserts disjointness and completeness; (3) scalers live inside `Pipeline`s fitted on
training rows; (4) the evaluation stage refuses to run unless `selection.json` was frozen on validation
profiles; (5) {{n_tests}} automated tests including leakage invariance (corrupting the measured internal
temperatures does not change predictions), causality, profile resets and streaming = offline.

**Run mode and sampling.** Mode: **{{mode_label}}**. Training profiles used: {{train_profiles_used}} of
{{n_train}}; history features computed at 2 Hz *before* thinning; training rows kept every {{stride}} samples
(effective interval {{interval}} s) → {{train_rows}} of {{train_rows_all}} training rows ({{kept_pct}} %).
Windows keep their physical duration. Validation and test use **all** rows of their profiles.

**Tuning.** LightGBM random search with {{trials}} configurations per track (trial 0 = library defaults),
early stopping on the validation profiles (a mild optimism for those models on the validation score, never on
