## 13. Thermal residual monitoring (experimental)

$$\text{residual}_t = y^{measured}_t - \hat y_t \quad(\text{Track B}),\qquad \bar r_t=\text{causal rolling mean over }{{smooth_s}}\text{ s}$$

The band is the {{band_q}}th percentile of $|\bar r|$ on the **validation** profiles: **±{{band}} °C**. An alarm
is raised when $|\bar r|$ stays outside the band for ≥ {{persist_s}} s, so isolated noisy samples do not trigger it.

| Healthy held-out data | Validation (calibration) | Test |
|---|---|---|
| samples outside band (raw residual) | {{val_raw}} % | {{test_raw}} % |
| samples outside band (smoothed) | {{val_smooth}} % | {{test_smooth}} % |
| time in persistent alarm | {{val_alarm}} % | {{test_alarm}} % |
| profiles with ≥ 1 alarm | {{val_prof_alarm}} / {{n_val}} | {{test_prof_alarm}} / {{n_test}} |
| alarm events per hour | {{val_events}} | {{test_events}} |

All alarms on this data are false alarms or ordinary model error (the profiles are healthy recordings), so the
transfer of the band from validation to test is the honest indicator of its reliability: {{monitor_transfer_text}}

